==============================================
IDEAL CUSTOMER PROFILE (ICP) ANALYSIS
==============================================

Client: Acme Corporation
Date: January 10, 2026
Analyst: Lead Gen Team

COMPANY FIRMOGRAPHICS:
✓ Annual Revenue: $10M - $100M
✓ Employee Count: 100 - 1,000 employees
✓ Industry: Manufacturing, Construction, Mining, Agriculture
✓ Geography: United States & Canada
✓ Equipment Fleet: 50+ heavy equipment units

TECHNOGRAPHICS:
- Uses ERP systems (SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics)
- Has equipment management software
- Active on LinkedIn
- Digital presence (website, social media)

BEHAVIORAL SIGNALS:
- Recent equipment purchases
- Attending industry trade shows
- Job postings for equipment managers
- Mentions of fleet expansion in press releases
- Active maintenance contracts

DECISION-MAKER PERSONAS:

1. Equipment Manager
   - Oversees day-to-day equipment operations
   - Pain point: Equipment downtime costs
   - Goal: Maximize equipment uptime

2. Procurement Director
   - Manages vendor relationships
   - Pain point: Supplier reliability
   - Goal: Cost optimization

3. Operations Executive (VP/Director)
   - Strategic equipment decisions
   - Pain point: ROI on equipment investments
   - Goal: Operational efficiency

DISQUALIFICATION CRITERIA:
✗ Companies with fewer than 50 equipment units
✗ Retail or service-only businesses
✗ Recent bankruptcy or financial distress
✗ Existing competitors' clients under contract

MESSAGING ANGLES BY PERSONA:
- Equipment Managers: "Reduce downtime by 40%"
- Procurement: "Cut maintenance costs by $200K annually"
- Executives: "Improve equipment ROI by 25%"

This document demonstrates the ICP analysis format used in your campaigns.
